@bio:

Alexander Morgan (Ph.D., McGill University, 2017) is a
Renaissance counterpoint researcher who specializes in
interval succession treatises and automated syntactical
analysis of scores in symbolic notation. Alexander
currently works outside of academia as a programmer, but
has contributed to several projects as a music information
retrieval consultant, including The Josquin Research
Project, VIS, CRIM, pyAMPACT, and now the Tasso in Music
Project. His greatest contributions to the field have been
in defining contrapuntal events theoretically and in code
for use in corpus studies and stylistically informed
research tools.


@@END: BIO